      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62b61f8ec938a62475e4cd14|full_name} Hue Shift is great, and the mask is good, but I noticed while you can select what color channel to use on the mask, you can only use one at a time (which makes selecting one seem a bit redundant). Any chance we can get different hue shifts by color channel? So we could put hair on G, clothes on R, skin on B for instance and give users a lot of customization on the same material.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-05-11T00:13:23.809Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Please add the option to:\n\nEnable Vertex Colors\n\nLike every other Shader in VRChat/Mobile even if it's a toggle.\n\nDetail Maps with MultiplyX2\n\nYou have Multiple Options Except the one Standard Lite uses.\n\nA Mask for HUE Shifting (and probably a way to Alter Emission Hue)\n\nYou want more people to be optimized, but you don't make masks that help people keep Material Counts down.\n\nA few of the current deal breakers for me at the moment.",
